/* The page gutter: the inset a page's chrome and content share, so a brand, a heading and a grid
   all start on one left edge. One custom property, `--page-gutter`, read by three utilities.

   A shell SETS the property once (the Hexline demo shell does, in src/demo/DemoLayout.tsx: 1rem,
   and 4rem from `lg`); everything inside reads it. Nothing inside a page ever writes a gutter of
   its own. Unset, it is 1rem, which is what an organism shown alone on a docs page gets.

   `px-gutter` for a box that holds content, `mx-gutter` for a box that must not be padded (a
   heading whose top rule starts at the gutter). A slider that runs edge to edge passes the same
   value, `var(--page-gutter, 1rem)`, to Carousel's `gutter`. */
@utility px-gutter {
  padding-inline: var(--page-gutter, 1rem);
}
@utility mx-gutter {
  margin-inline: var(--page-gutter, 1rem);
}
